# SKMS marketing voice

When writing or editing marketing copy for Scot Krav Maga / SKMS (organic social, ads, events, site CTAs):

## Who we are

- We do not baby people.
- We go in, teach with maximum efficiency, empower people, go hard, and get out.
- Motto when it fits: Stay Safe, Get Fit, Hit Hard.

## Do

- Announce clearly: what it is, when, where, price, come along.
- Short punchy openers are fine (e.g. `Women-only beginners self defence — January.`).
- Invite with **Come along.**
- Name the work: efficient, practical training; awareness, boundaries, skills that work.
- Empowerment language that implies effort is good: challenge yourself, leave more empowered, put the work in and get stronger.
- Keep facts tight: dates, venue, price, book links.
- UK spelling: self defence.

## Do not

- Hype questions: “Want self defence that actually works?”, “Ready to…?”, soft quiz-style openers.
- Babying / hand-holding: we’ll look after you, safe supportive space framing as the sell, “all fitness levels we’ll take care of you”.
- Scripted marketer cadence or exclamation-heavy promo speak.
- Rely on member referral blasts — historically almost never convert for this club.

## Structure that works (from kept posts)

1. What it is (short line or one sentence)
2. Come along + what you train / get (efficient, practical, challenge, empower)
3. Logistics (when, where, price)
4. Book links
5. Motto optional

## Ads vs organic

- Organic: club voice above.
- Paid Meta: still direct and factual; short primary text OK; avoid soft babysitting even in ads.
